    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33143" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossŭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		2. os, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for bones</i>, <i>bone-</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">OLLA OSSVARIA,</span>”
				<i>a vase to contain the bones of a corpse</i>, <i>a
						bone-urn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2896</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossŭārĭum</span></b>  (also written
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossārĭum</span></b> ), ii,
			n., <i>a receptacle for the bones of the
				dead</i>, <i>a bone-vault</i>, <i>charnel-house</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 47, 12, 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4511</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">4556</span></i>.</div>
